From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lawrence Chen <lawrencecchen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 09:14:07 +0000
Subject: fix: support Electron printing APIs in Chrome runtime

Electron adds UpdatePrintSettings to PrintManagerHost and disables Chrome enterprise print content analysis, but the full Chrome browser source set also builds headless and print-preview implementations that must match that surface. Implement the unsupported headless endpoint, use Chromium 152 current frame APIs, include the complete query queue type, and consistently disable the unsupported enterprise setter call sites. This is Electron-specific and cannot be upstreamed because upstream does not have the Electron UpdatePrintSettings Mojo method.

